From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: guard ethtool callbacks against missing phylink

Since phylink is now set up after register_netdev() in
edma_port_setup(), ppe_port->phylink is still NULL for a short time
after the netdev becomes visible.  The ethtool callbacks for link
settings and pause parameters pass it to phylink without checking, and
would dereference a NULL pointer if called in that window.

Return -EOPNOTSUPP from the callbacks that return a value, and skip the
call in edma_get_pauseparam(), when phylink is not available.  This
matches edma_port_open(), edma_port_close() and edma_port_ioctl(),
which already check ppe_port->phylink.

Signed-off-by: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_ethtool.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_ethtool.c
@@ -203,6 +203,9 @@ static int edma_get_link_ksettings(struct net_device *netdev,
 	if (!port_priv)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (!port->phylink)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	return phylink_ethtool_ksettings_get(port->phylink, cmd);
 }
 
@@ -215,6 +218,9 @@ static int edma_set_link_ksettings(struct net_device *netdev,
 	if (!port_priv)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (!port->phylink)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	return phylink_ethtool_ksettings_set(port->phylink, cmd);
 }
 
@@ -227,7 +233,8 @@ static void edma_get_pauseparam(struct net_device *netdev,
 	if (!port_priv)
 		return;
 
-	phylink_ethtool_get_pauseparam(port->phylink, pause);
+	if (port->phylink)
+		phylink_ethtool_get_pauseparam(port->phylink, pause);
 }
 
 static int edma_set_pauseparam(struct net_device *netdev,
@@ -239,6 +246,9 @@ static int edma_set_pauseparam(struct net_device *netdev,
 	if (!port_priv)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (!port->phylink)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	return phylink_ethtool_set_pauseparam(port->phylink, pause);
 }
 
